# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working tree
# to CRLF at checkout. That is not cosmetic here. This repository compares
# generated content against committed content byte for byte:
# `generate-compatibility.mjs --check` reads compatibility.json as text and
# compares it to freshly generated JSON, and every evidence report is verified
# against a self-hash of its own canonical bytes.
#
# A CRLF checkout makes the committed file differ from anything generated at run
# time, so `compatibility:check` reported the file as stale on Windows while it
# was perfectly current — a false failure that says nothing about the product.
* text=auto eol=lf
